# What does NOT ship in the .vsix.
#
# ⚠️ This file decides what strangers receive. Getting it wrong produces the single most likely failure
# mode for this extension: it installs, activates, and then does nothing — because something the engine
# needs at runtime was excluded. `npm run package` verifies the result; `npx @vscode/vsce ls` shows it.

# ── secrets: never, under any pattern, from anywhere ──
# vsce's own check caught `packages/orchestrator/.env` (a REAL API key) being pulled in through the
# workspace dependency graph before `--no-dependencies` was added. One guard is not enough for a secret:
# these rules, `--no-dependencies`, and an independent scan in scripts/build-engine.js all have to agree.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*

# The 32px render is a design check — it documents that the mark survives the size the marketplace
# list actually uses. It belongs in the repo, not in every user's download.
media/icon-32-preview.png

# ── build inputs (the .vsix ships dist/, never sources) ──
src/**
test/**
scripts/**
out/**
**/*.ts
**/*.map
**/tsconfig.json
**/eslint.config.mjs
esbuild.js
.gitignore
.yarnrc
vsc-extension-quickstart.md
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
**/.vscode-test.*

# ── dependencies ──
# Everything the engine imports is bundled into dist/orchestrator.js. The ONE exception is
# `@playwright/mcp`, which the engine SPAWNS as a child process and therefore cannot be inlined — it is
# staged into `dist/node_modules/` by scripts/build-engine.js, which is the first place Node looks when
# resolving from `dist/orchestrator.js`.
#
# The extension's own node_modules is excluded wholesale. It holds only devDependencies, and packaging
# it is what let a trial build reach `../../node_modules/agenticqa` and, through it, a real `.env`.
node_modules/**

# Trim the shipped packages: none of this is needed to run them, and playwright-core carries a lot of it.
dist/node_modules/**/*.map
dist/node_modules/**/test/**
dist/node_modules/**/tests/**
dist/node_modules/**/*.md
